<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!--
    GonogoRealAntennasUplink's OWN contract slice: the three RA-only wire payload
    types that used to sit inside mod/Sitrep.Contract/Comms.cs, relocated here per
    the operator mandate that NO uplink-specific wire type may live in core, even
    for an in-monorepo Uplink (see
    local_docs/design/2026-08-10-uplink-types-out-of-core-plan.md). Seventh and
    LAST step of that plan, and the only one the plan sequenced separately,
    because it is a PARTIAL extract from a shared-shape file rather than a
    whole-file move.

    The three: CommsLinkQuality (comms.linkQuality), CommsDataRate
    (comms.dataRate), CommsLinkMargin (comms.linkMargin). Recounted from
    RtConfig.wirePayloadTypes rather than trusted, and three is what it is: the
    first slice whose inventory the plan had right. No enum moves with them (all
    four comms enums are referenced by types that stay core), so this slice needs
    no enum codegen leg.

    WHAT STAYED, and why the boundary falls where it does. comms.* is a
    two-provider channel family: Gonogo.KSP/CommsCoreUplink.cs owns the shared
    shape and the elected backend sources it (stock CommNet, or this Uplink's
    RaCommsBackend when RealAntennas is installed). So CommsConnectivity /
    CommsSignalStrength / CommsControlState / CommsPath / CommsNetwork /
    CommsDelay / CommsLink, their nested CommsHop / CommsNetworkNode /
    CommsNetworkEdge, the four enums, and the ICommsBackend capability interface
    this Uplink IMPLEMENTS from outside are all core, and stay. Only the three
    channels this Uplink declares in its OWN manifest and publishes itself moved.

    The sharpest case is CommsHop.BandRateBitsPerSec, which Comms.cs itself
    documents as "the RealAntennas-only per-hop rate annotation": absent under
    bare CommNet. It stays core regardless, because it is a nullable FIELD on a
    SHARED type rather than a type of its own. Extracting it would fork the one
    shape both backends fill. RA-only presence is not RA-only ownership, and that
    distinction is what makes this a partial extract rather than a file move.

    Deliberately its own small project rather than folding into
    GonogoRealAntennasUplink.csproj: that one is net48-only and reaches into a
    KSP/Unity reference set (UnityEngine, Assembly-CSharp, stock CommNet) that
    rtcli could not load. These three types are plain DTOs touching nothing but
    Sitrep.Contract, so the split keeps the codegen input clean. The dual-target
    boilerplate below stays a straight copy of Sitrep.Contract.csproj's.

    MIT, matching GonogoRealAntennasUplink.csproj and needing none of the
    deliberation the two GPL slices in this repo took: this Uplink is MIT because
    it never links RealAntennas at all (every RA member is reached by runtime
    reflection, the arm's-length pattern its own csproj header explains), and
    nothing in THIS project even reflects. RA's attribution stays in
    ../GonogoRealAntennasUplink/NOTICE-REALANTENNAS.txt.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net48</TargetFrameworks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <AssemblyName>GonogoRealAntennasUplink.Contract</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Gonogo.RealAntennasUplink</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Reinforced.Typings is a compile-time-only codegen dependency: rtcli
       reads the [TsInterface] attributes baked into this assembly's metadata
       to generate this Uplink's own TS SDK slice (see codegen.sh). Must NOT
       flow to net48 (the runtime TFM GonogoRealAntennasUplink.csproj bundles):
       same PrivateAssets/Condition/#if NETSTANDARD2_0 discipline as
       Sitrep.Contract.csproj, for the identical reason (a KSP-loaded net48
       assembly must never try to resolve Reinforced.Typings.dll). -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Reinforced.Typings" Version="1.6.7" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0'" PrivateAssets="all" IncludeAssets="compile;build;native;contentfiles;analyzers;buildtransitive" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Sitrep.Contract only, Private="false": SitrepContractAttribute/
       SitrepTopicAttribute/SitrepUnitAttribute/Units/PayloadMeta are core's
       cross-package surface, provided by the core mod (GonogoCore) at runtime,
       never copied here. Same pattern GonogoRealAntennasUplink.csproj already
       uses for its own Sitrep.Contract reference. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Sitrep.Contract\Sitrep.Contract.csproj">
      <Private>false</Private>
    </ProjectReference>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
